Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Pointer defaults. The pointer shadow is on: the Pointer tab's "Enable pointer shadow" box is SPI_GETCURSORSHADOW, bit 0x2000 of the
; DWORD HKCU\Control Panel\Desktop\UserPreferencesMask (the second byte's 0x20). The stock value is 10,00,00,80 (gradient captions and
; UI effects) and has the bit off, so the box is clear; this sets 0x2000 and nothing else.
;
; The scheme list is the user's schemes (HKCU\Control Panel\Cursors\Schemes, where Afterglow is) followed by the system schemes in
; HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Control Panel\Cursors\Schemes, each with " (system scheme)" added, then "(None)". The
; applet skips a value whose data is empty, so the one stock system scheme, "ReactOS Default", is emptied and the list is "Afterglow"
; and "(None)".
;
; (c) Copyright 2026 Liminal HQ, Scott Morris
; SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 OR MIT

[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Control Panel\Desktop]
"UserPreferencesMask"=hex:10,20,00,80

[HKEY_USERS\.DEFAULT\Control Panel\Desktop]
"UserPreferencesMask"=hex:10,20,00,80

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Control Panel\Cursors\Schemes]
"ReactOS Default"=""
